                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "First of all, it's probably important to say you're getting VR cricket for £3.99 here, so it's hard to have too many issues with this game.\n\nPros:\n- Gameplay itself is pretty solid - I edge the ball a lot so it must be realistic.\n- Touch support works well.\n- Replays look nice and give you a chance to see how wrong your technique was.\n- Dev responds to feedback (see comments).\n\nCons (fixed since writing review):\n- Quite a lot of the balls are pitched short, making it hard to drive. On the plus side, my hook shot is looking a lot better nowadays.\n- Menu system could do with a bit of work, quit and continue buttons are close together which means I have mistakenly quit games halfway through.\n\nOverall, worth picking up for the price if you're into the sport.",
